<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Deliberately empty. The hardened runtime is on; every entitlement is a
	  hole in it, and nothing here needs one.

	  Not sandboxed. The Mac App Store is out: this app must spawn docker and
	  ssh, and later a login shell. Spawning children needs no entitlement
	  outside a sandbox, and a sandbox entitlement such as
	  com.apple.security.network.client does nothing without
	  com.apple.security.app-sandbox — it would read as protection that is
	  not there.

	  No com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit. WKWebView's JavaScript JIT runs in
	  Apple's own com.apple.WebKit.WebContent.xpc, which carries that
	  entitlement under Apple's signature; granting it here would let *our*
	  process map writable-executable memory for nothing.

	  No com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation either, though the
	  frozen daemon is the obvious candidate. It does not need it: PyInstaller
	  ad-hoc signs its own tree, and the daemon is a separate process that
	  does not inherit this app's hardened runtime. Verified by signing a
	  bundle with an empty plist and watching it spawn the frozen daemon,
	  serve /health and probe containers.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
